  v1.28.0 were all prerelease=false draft=false and days newer -- the state
  PMAT-534 was filed from.

  The `nightly` row is the case the arm must NOT refuse: a deliberate rolling
  prerelease, which GitHub will never make latest.
### 2. why clearing the flag is not enough
  A release is born a DRAFT PRERELEASE (.github/workflows/release.yml, PMAT-166)
  so no consumer sees a half-uploaded asset set, and the publish job un-drafts it
  while LEAVING it a prerelease:
    548:              gh release edit "$RELEASE_TAG" --draft=false --prerelease --repo "${{ github.repository }}"
  GitHub fixes "latest" when the prerelease flag is WRITTEN and never recomputes
  it, so a later `gh release edit <tag> --prerelease=false` clears the flag and
  leaves the pointer where it was. The promotion must say `--latest`.

